# Code Style Standards

## TypeScript

- Use strict TypeScript, avoid `any` types
- Prefer named exports over default exports
- Use async/await over raw promises
- Define interfaces for all data shapes

## React

- Use functional components with hooks
- Prefer composition over inheritance
- Co-locate component tests with source files
- Use ErrorBoundary for error handling

## Naming Conventions

- Components: PascalCase (`UserProfile.tsx`)
- Hooks: camelCase with `use` prefix (`useForm.ts`)
- Utilities: camelCase (`formatDate.ts`)
- Types/Interfaces: PascalCase (`CustomerData`)
- Constants: SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE

## Imports

- Group imports: React, external libs, internal modules, types
- Use absolute imports from `src/`
- Avoid circular dependencies
